# Copy to .env before running `make up`. These are development defaults only.

# --- Database ---
# Local dev uses the POSTGRES_* parts below. For managed Postgres (Supabase),
# set a full URL instead — it takes precedence over the POSTGRES_* parts:
#   App pool via the Transaction pooler (6543), pooler-safe pgx:
# ORAKO_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<PROJECT_REF>:<PASSWORD>@aws-0-<REGION>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
# ORAKO_PG_TX_POOLER=true
#   Migrations need a session/direct connection (Session pooler, 5432):
# ORAKO_MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<PROJECT_REF>:<PASSWORD>@aws-0-<REGION>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# --- Postgres (local dev) ---
POSTGRES_USER=orako
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=orako
POSTGRES_DB=orako
# Host bind port (container always listens on 5432).
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
# Host value; docker-compose overrides this to the service name for orako_server.
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost

# --- orako-server ---
ORAKO_HTTP_PORT=8080
LOG_LEVEL=info
# Encrypts integration credentials at rest. Required outside development mode.
# Generate once with: openssl rand -base64 32
# ORAKO_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Auth (ORAKO_AUTH_MODE: dev | oidc | local) ---
# dev  : unsigned dev-stub token — LOCAL ONLY (default).
# oidc : verify JWTs against an OIDC issuer's JWKS (Supabase in SaaS).
# local: HS256 shared secret, server is its own IdP (self-host). deploy/bootstrap.sh
#        sets this up for you.
ORAKO_AUTH_MODE=dev
# ORAKO_AUTH_ISSUER=https://<PROJECT_REF>.supabase.co/auth/v1
# ORAKO_AUTH_AUDIENCE=authenticated
# First admin for local mode, seeded once on boot (idempotent). Log in with these,
# then invite teammates (needs SMTP). No-op after the account exists.
# ORAKO_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# ORAKO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<a strong password>
# Reset/invite links + session tokens are signed with this; keep it stable after
# first boot (changing it logs everyone out).
# Supabase service_role key (Settings → API). Optional: when set, invitation
# emails carry a signed link that logs the invitee in directly (no second
# email verification). Never commit the real key.
# ORAKO_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# Dashboard build args (compose overlay / task saas): bake the embedded UI in
# OIDC mode. Publishable pair only — public by design.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<PROJECT_REF>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxx
# ORAKO_AUTH_HS256_SECRET=

# --- Attachments (S3-compatible object storage) ---
# Files/images that agents and humans exchange. Unset ORAKO_S3_ENDPOINT =
# attachments disabled entirely (upload returns a clear error, inbound files are
# dropped, text still flows). Works with any S3-compatible store; for Supabase
# Storage the endpoint is the project's /storage/v1/s3 path and the credentials
# are DEDICATED S3 access keys (Storage → S3 Connection → New access key), NOT
# the service_role key. Create the bucket first. Never commit the real secret.
# ORAKO_S3_ENDPOINT=https://<PROJECT_REF>.supabase.co/storage/v1/s3
# ORAKO_S3_REGION=<project region, e.g. eu-west-3>
# ORAKO_S3_BUCKET=orako-attachments
# ORAKO_S3_ACCESS_KEY=<S3 access key id>
# ORAKO_S3_SECRET_KEY=<S3 secret access key>
# ORAKO_ATTACHMENT_MAX_BYTES=26214400   # optional, default 25 MiB

# --- License / edition (self-host) ---
# The license key is NO LONGER an env var. Obtain a signed key from the hosted
# licensing service, then paste it in the dashboard under Settings → License: it is
# stored in the DB and applies instantly (no restart). The signing public key is
# baked into the binary, so no key config is needed here. Verification is offline;
# the key auto-renews each billing period (set ORAKO_LICENSE_OFFLINE=true for an
# air-gapped install). Leave unlicensed to run the free Community edition.
# ORAKO_LICENSE_OFFLINE=        # set true to disable license auto-renewal (air-gapped)
